  "notes": "Nimbus, Boo and Meep now support stationary or scrolling custom text and locally uploaded images in the normal screen playlist. Scroll messages across the OLED, choose a speed, or keep text still with alignment and border controls. PNG, JPG and still WebP images convert locally to 128 × 64 monochrome pixels, with fit/crop, shading and inversion controls.\n\nName, preview, reorder and set the duration of your image screens. Save still text, faces and images to compatible droids for wall power. Scrolling requires the app running. Claw stays focused on Claude/Codex usage.\n\nExisting screens and profiles are preserved. Settings migrate to schema 3 with a private backup; older apps refuse this newer format. No firmware change is required, including on swapped-wiring droids.\n\nMac and Windows support signed in-app updates; Linux uses the packages below. Mac notarization and Windows publisher signing remain separate from updater signatures.\n",
